_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 10
---
order: 10
---
short_label: X.10
---
statement: To find two straight lines incommensurable, the one in length only, and the other in square also, with an assigned straight line.
---
red_highlight: yes
---
proof:

Let *A* be the assigned straight line.

It is required to find two straight lines incommensurable, the one in length only, and the other in square also, with *A.*

Set out two numbers *B* and *C* which do not have to one another the ratio which a square number has to a square number, that is, which are not similar plane numbers, and let it be contrived that *B* is to *C* as the square on *A* is to the square on *D,* for we have learned how to do this. [!just X.6.Cor]

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="180" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
